    "created_at": "2019-11-07T00:51:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-07T00:51:41Z",
    "body": "> Any observations about implementations choosing to go for persistent permissions? Why leaving it to implementations?\r\n\r\nI've updated the answer to this question with our experience from initially shipping Web Bluetooth without support for persistent permissions. The precise details of how permissions are managed is left up to implementations because this is an area of active research and implementations should be given room to innovate without being tied to particular behavior by individual specifications. If such behavior were to be prescribed it should be part of the Permissions API specification.",
