    "body": "Thanks for clarifying the 'expectation issue'.\r\n\r\nNow with (https://github.com/WICG/serial/commit/0ab4392ec6e6c105b4e6086b39510496648f71df) \r\n\r\n> For frequently visited sites experience with other APIs such as Web Bluetooth shows that users prefer not to be asked to grant the same permission for every session\r\n\r\nI'm wondering if adding a comment that explicitly states this is a work-in-progress (i.e. unstable) and linking to other similar specs (here Web Bluetooth; another story is this \"experience\" is not clear to the reader) is a good idea. ",
